  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Welcome back, Digital Explorer!"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "Last week you read tables and bar charts.\n\nThis week you become a data scientist.\n\nYou will collect data, find the middle and spot charts that cheat."
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "emoji": "📊",
   "alt": "Data scientists collect facts and look for stories in the numbers.",
   "caption": "Data scientists collect facts and look for stories in the numbers."
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Stop 1: Collecting data"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "A **survey** asks many people the same question. We record each answer with a **tally** mark.\n\nA fair question has clear choices. Ask lots of people, not just your best friend, to get a fair picture."
  },
  {
   "type": "chart",
   "kind": "tally",
   "title": "A survey: favourite fruit at Eid party",
   "rows": [
    {
     "label": "Mango",
     "value": 7
    },
    {
     "label": "Apple",
     "value": 4
    },
    {
     "label": "Dates",
     "value": 5
    },
    {
     "label": "Banana",
     "value": 2
    }
   ],
   "caption": "Each stroke is one vote. Bundles of five make counting quick."
  },
  {
   "type": "check",
   "question": {
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "prompt": "Which survey question is the clearest?",
    "hint": "It should have clear choices.",
    "options": [
     {
      "id": "a",
      "text": "What is the best thing ever?"
     },
     {
      "id": "b",
      "text": "Which fruit do you like best: mango, apple, dates or banana?"
     },
     {
      "id": "c",
      "text": "Do you like stuff?"
     }
    ],
    "answer": [
     "b"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "activity",
   "title": "Class survey",
   "materials": [
    "Paper and pencil",
    "Family or friends to ask"
   ],
   "instructions": [
    "Think of a question with 3 or 4 choices, like 'Which pet do you like best?'",
    "Ask at least 10 people and make a tally mark for each answer.",
    "Count the marks. Which choice won?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "text": "Stop 2: Mode and range"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "The **mode** is the value that appears most often. In 2, 3, 3, 4, 3 the mode is 3.\n\nThe **range** shows how spread out the data is. It is the biggest number take away the smallest."
  },
  {
   "type": "chart",
   "kind": "bar_chart",
   "title": "Goals scored in 6 matches",
   "rows": [
    {
     "label": "Match 1",
     "value": 2
    },
    {
     "label": "Match 2",
     "value": 3
    },
    {
     "label": "Match 3",
     "value": 3
    },
    {
     "label": "Match 4",
     "value": 5
    },
    {
     "label": "Match 5",
     "value": 3
    },
    {
     "label": "Match 6",
     "value": 1
    }
   ],
   "caption": "3 goals appears three times, so the mode is 3. The range is 5 - 1 = 4."
  },
  {
   "type": "check",
   "question": {
    "type": "number",
    "prompt": "Find the mode of 4, 6, 4, 5, 4, 7.",
    "hint": "Which number appears most?",
    "answer": {
     "value": 4,
     "tolerance": 0
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "check",
   "question": {
    "type": "number",
